WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.158
Your AI agents don't just answer questions anymore.

2
00:00:04.158 --> 00:00:07.619
They issue refunds, grant access, and move data.

3
00:00:08.317 --> 00:00:11.745
But most of them act on whatever access they were given.

4
00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:14.799
No one checks first, and nothing records why.

5
00:00:15.483 --> 00:00:19.608
AgentPermit puts a checkpoint between your agents and your systems.

6
00:00:19.608 --> 00:00:22.001
Every agent, explicitly permitted.

7
00:00:22.717 --> 00:00:24.600
Before it acts, the agent asks.

8
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:30.369
AgentPermit knows who's asking from the agent's sign-in, not from what the request claims.

9
00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:33.116
Your rules decide every request.

10
00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:35.403
Routine actions go straight through.

11
00:00:35.403 --> 00:00:37.164
Risky ones are stopped.

12
00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:42.005
Anything in between waits for a named person.

13
00:00:42.005 --> 00:00:47.823
The request stays frozen until they approve or reject it, in the console or in Teams.

14
00:00:49.083 --> 00:00:50.787
And there's no way around it.

15
00:00:50.787 --> 00:00:54.789
Your systems only accept actions that come through AgentPermit.

16
00:00:56.083 --> 00:01:00.076
Every decision leaves a signed receipt, chained to the one before.

17
00:01:00.076 --> 00:01:01.588
Change one, and it shows.

18
00:01:01.588 --> 00:01:04.549
And anyone with the public key can check it.

19
00:01:06.083 --> 00:01:11.765
It runs in your own Azure tenant, and works with Copilot Studio, your own code, and MCP.

20
00:01:11.765 --> 00:01:13.679
Your data stays with you.

21
00:01:14.883 --> 00:01:17.053
AgentPermit, from Plinthera.

22
00:01:17.053 --> 00:01:20.761
Book your demo at plinthera.com/agentpermit.
